  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Quiet Exam Hall",
    "overview": "TryOutKu looks and behaves like a first-party Apple product, in two worlds. The landing page and the score moment are dark and cinematic: a black ground, iOS dark surfaces, and app screens glowing inside device frames. The working pages (catalog, exam, leaderboard, admin) are light: pale gray and white grounds, near-black ink. One action blue carries every primary action in both. The exam interface is treated as the product: the landing shows it the way Apple shows hardware, on a laptop whose lid opens as you scroll and whose screen runs a playable exam, flanked by a tablet (the catalog) and a phone (the score). The app screens borrow iOS and macOS structure (large titles, grouped inset lists, sheets, segmented controls, a source-list sidebar) so a visitor knows where everything is before noticing the style.\n\nDensity is low on public pages and moderate in the app. Color is reserved for state: green for answered and correct, orange for remaining time and \"ragu-ragu\" (unsure), red for the last minute and destructive actions, gold, silver and bronze for the top three ranks. Each catalog gets an iOS-hue cover with a cropped monogram, because there are no uploaded covers.\n\nThe old look (cream paper, Lora serif, gold underline, emoji icons) is retired and should not come back.",
